
(..0.29999) Clouds pour all day onto muddied fields; banners droop and soak through. We hope the weather is better next year.
(0.3..0.49999) The weather isn't quite with us this year. It stays cold and cloudy all day.
(0.5..0.69999) The rain mostly holds off. Moments of sunshine keeps spirits high.
(0.7..0.79999) It is cool but bright. Flags snap in the wind and the march keeps good pace.
(0.8..0.89999) It is near-perfect May Day weather: clear skies, mild air, the sun shimmers through the flags.
(0.9..) The weather is unusually splendid. People linger in the parks long after the speeches, singing and talking into the evening.
